---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';
import { SITE_CONFIG } from '../lib/config';
import { useTranslation, getLocaleFromUrl, getLocalizedPath } from '../i18n/utils';
import type { Locale } from '../i18n/languages';

interface Props {
  locale?: Locale;
}

const { locale } = Astro.props;
const currentLocale = locale || getLocaleFromUrl(Astro.url);
const t = useTranslation(currentLocale);
const contactUrl = getLocalizedPath('/contact/', currentLocale);
const privacyUrl = getLocalizedPath('/privacy-policy/', currentLocale);
---

<ContentLayout
  title={t.pages.terms.title}
  description={t.pages.terms.description}
  locale={currentLocale}
  keywords="disposable email service, temporary email generator, receive only temp mail, developer api terms"
>
  <p>
    <strong>Last Updated:</strong> October 21, 2026
  </p>

  <p>
    These Terms of Service ("Terms") are an agreement between you ("you") and <strong>TempoEmails</strong> ("we", "us", "our") covering your use of the website at <strong>{SITE_CONFIG.domain}</strong> and its temporary email features (the "Service").
  </p>

  <p>
    By using TempoEmails you agree to these Terms. <strong>If you don't agree, don't use the Service.</strong>
  </p>

  <blockquote>
    <strong>Summary:</strong> TempoEmails is a free, receive-only temporary email service built on third-party mail providers. We don't guarantee that mail will arrive or how long it will be kept. Don't use it for anything illegal, abusive or fraudulent.
  </blockquote>

  <h2>1. Description of Service</h2>
  <p>
    TempoEmails gives you temporary email addresses for receiving confirmation links, one-time passcodes (OTPs) and similar short-lived messages, so you don't have to give out your personal or work address. The addresses are created at third-party providers (Mail.tm, Mail.gw, Inboxes, TempMail.lol and Guerrilla Mail) and shown in our web interface.
  </p>
  <p>
    In particular:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Receive-only:</strong> you can read, download and delete messages, but you can't send or reply from a TempoEmails address.</li>
    <li><strong>Temporary:</strong> the provider that hosts an address decides how long it and its messages are kept, and may delete them at any time. Messages you've received are also cached in your browser until you delete them.</li>
    <li><strong>No account:</strong> you don't register with us. Mail.tm and Mail.gw inboxes come with a generated password; inboxes from the other providers have none and can be read by anyone who knows the address.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Acceptable Use Policy</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to use TempoEmails in line with the laws that apply to you, and only for legitimate purposes such as protecting your main address, testing software or receiving one-off verification emails.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Prohibited Activities</h2>
  <p>
    You may not use the Service for:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Fraud and illegal activity:</strong> including payment fraud, identity theft, money laundering or illegal trade.</li>
    <li><strong>Phishing and malware:</strong> including phishing campaigns, social engineering or spreading malicious software.</li>
    <li><strong>Attacking the Service:</strong> flooding our server or the mail relay, trying to get around its rate limits, or using it to reach anything other than the supported mail providers.</li>
    <li><strong>Evading other platforms' rules:</strong> using temporary addresses to repeatedly get around bans, rate limits, trial limits or security controls in breach of that platform's terms.</li>
    <li><strong>Harassment:</strong> including stalking, threats, defamation or hate speech.</li>
    <li><strong>Bulk creation:</strong> using bots or scripts to create inboxes in bulk or to scrape the Service.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>4. Service Availability, Changes, and Termination</h2>
  <p>
    The Service depends on third-party mail providers, so you accept that:
  </p>
  <ol>
    <li>We may change, limit, suspend or end the Service, or any feature of it, at any time, with or without notice.</li>
    <li>Providers add and remove domains and may shut down or change their service. An address can stop receiving mail if its provider or domain goes away, and we may add or drop providers.</li>
    <li>We may block IP addresses that break these Terms or put the Service at risk.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>5. Intellectual Property Rights</h2>
  <p>
    The TempoEmails name, logo, design and code belong to TempoEmails or its licensors. We give you a limited, non-exclusive, non-transferable right to use the Service for personal or internal business purposes. Email content you receive belongs to its senders.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Disclaimer of Warranties</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>THE SERVICE IS PROVIDED ON AN "AS-IS" AND "AS-AVAILABLE" BASIS. TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, TEMPOEMAILS EXPRESSLY DISCLAIMS ALL WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, WHETHER EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO THE IMPLIED WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, AND NON-INFRINGEMENT.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    Without limiting the foregoing, we make no warranty that:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>The Service will meet your needs or be available at any given time.</li>
    <li>Emails will arrive, or arrive without delay or errors.</li>
    <li>Other websites will accept or send mail to the domains our providers offer.</li>
    <li>An inbox or its messages will remain available for any particular length of time.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>7. Limitation of Liability</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>IN NO EVENT SHALL TEMPOEMAILS, ITS DIRECTORS, EMPLOYEES, AFFILIATES, OR PARTNERS BE LIABLE TO YOU OR ANY THIRD PARTY FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, CONSEQUENTIAL, EXEMPLARY, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, INCLUDING LOST PROFITS, LOST REVENUE, LOSS OF DATA, OR INTERRUPTED COMMUNICATIONS ARISING FROM YOUR USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE THE SERVICE.</strong>
  </p>
  <p>
    You understand that many temporary inboxes can be read by anyone who knows the address, and that any inbox can disappear. <strong>You accept all risk of losing access to accounts you registered with a temporary address, including missed password-reset emails and expired verification links.</strong>
  </p>

  <h2>8. Indemnification</h2>
  <p>
    You agree to defend, indemnify, and hold harmless TempoEmails, its subsidiaries, affiliates, officers, and contractors from and against any claims, liabilities, damages, losses, and expenses (including reasonable attorney fees) arising out of or in any way connected with your breach of these Terms or your misuse of the Service.
  </p>

  <h2>9. Governing Law and Severability</h2>
  <p>
    These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the applicable laws of the jurisdiction in which TempoEmails operates, without regard to conflict of law principles. If any provision of these Terms is found to be unlawful, void, or unenforceable, that provision shall be deemed severable and shall not affect the validity and enforceability of any remaining provisions.
  </p>

  <h2>10. Modifications to Terms</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these Terms. Changes take effect when posted here, and the date at the top shows the latest version. If you keep using the Service after a change, you accept the updated Terms.
  </p>

  <h2>11. Contact Information</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about these Terms:
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href={`mailto:${SITE_CONFIG.emails.contact}`}>{SITE_CONFIG.emails.contact}</a></li>
    <li><strong>Support Desk:</strong> <a href={contactUrl}>Contact TempoEmails Support</a></li>
    <li><strong>Privacy Policy:</strong> <a href={privacyUrl}>Read Privacy Policy</a></li>
  </ul>
</ContentLayout>
